1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
This video explains how to configure SAML SSO using Active Directory Federation Services as your identity provider.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
You will also need to refer to the ADFS documentation.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:21,000
To add Berber Suite Enterprise Edition to your trusted applications,

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,000
log in to Berber Suite Enterprise Edition as an administrator.

5
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
From the settings menu, select Integrations.

6
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
On the SAML tile, click Configure.

7
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Notice that you can copy both the Relying Party Trust Identifier and the Relying Party Service URL.

8
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:43,000
In ADFS, run the Add Relying Party Trust Wizard.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Paste the Relying Party Service URL into the Relying Party SAML 2.0 SSO Service URL field.

10
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Paste the Relying Party Trust Identifier into the Relying Party Trust Identifier field.

11
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:04,000
To configure Berber Suite Enterprise Edition, you need to obtain some key details from ADFS.

12
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,000
For more information, refer to the ADFS documentation.

13
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:11,000
You need to obtain the following details.

14
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:16,000
The Entity ID, the SSO URL, and the Token Signing Certificate.

15
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:25,000
To enter the key details in Berber Suite Enterprise Edition, ensure that you're still on the SAML page.

16
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:28,000
In Company Details, enter your company name.

17
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Enter the key details in the relevant fields, and click Save.

18
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:42,000
To make sure that the group membership of your users is sent to Berber Suite Enterprise Edition in a format that you can recognize, you have the following options.

19
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:49,000
Create a central claim insurance policy that sends all of your groups to Berber Suite Enterprise Edition automatically.

20
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:55,000
To expose all of your users groups to Berber Suite Enterprise Edition, configure a central claim issuance policy.

21
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:59,000
This allows you to manage the claim rules for all of your groups in one place.

22
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:03,000
It also removes the need to configure claim rules each time you add the new group.

23
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Please refer to our documentation guide for rule examples.

24
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Your second option is to configure claim rules for each group that you want to expose to Berber Suite Enterprise Edition individually.

25
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:20,000
This gives you more granular control over which groups and related information are exposed to Berber Suite Enterprise Edition in each claim.

26
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:24,000
We provide steps to help you configure this in our online documentation.

27
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:28,000
It's worth noting that you can also use a combination of both approaches.

28
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:34,000
In this case, the groups available to Berber Suite Enterprise Edition would be the union of the groups covered by the claim issuance policy,

29
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:39,000
and any additional groups for which you have created individual claim rules.

30
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,000
The group will be the union of the group that you have created individual claim rules for the claim rules.

